    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **278 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**, including the new `Cp13Tests`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the \"reject creating an owner once 20 have been created today (by registration date), respond 400\" rule as an OfficeFloor function-injection step, following the existing reject-step pattern (`RejectDuplicateOwner`).\n\nFiles added:\n- `RejectDailyOwnerLimit.java` \u2014 counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals `LocalDate.now()`; throws `DailyOwnerLimitException` when the count has already reached 20 (the new owner isn't saved yet, so the 21st create sees exactly 20 and is rejected).\n- `DailyOwnerLimitException.java` \u2014 checked exception so it appears in the `throws` clause.\n- `DailyOwnerLimitExceptionHandler.java` \u2014 responds `400 Bad Request` with a `ProblemDetail` body, mirroring the other escalation handlers.\n- `escalation/\u2026DailyOwnerLimitException.yml` \u2014 wires the exception to its handler.\n\nFile changed:\n- `rest/api/owners.POST.yml` \u2014 inserted a `rejectDailyLimit` step (under `transaction` governance) into the POST pipeline, after `normalizeCity` and before the duplicate checks.\n\nSince owners get today's registration date by default (`BuildOwner`) and the test uses distinct cities, only the daily cap is exercised \u2014 the 21st create today returns 400.",
